---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Base title="Urban Mobility" description="Matthew Rossi's engagement with urban mobility, transit advocacy, and civic technology.">

  <div class="page">
  <PageHeader title="Urban Mobility" description="Advocacy, civic tech, and self-directed work in transit and urban systems." />

  <section aria-labelledby="civic-tech-heading">
    <h2 id="civic-tech-heading">Civic Technology</h2>
    <p>Living in Chicago, I got involved with <a href="https://chihacknight.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChiHackNight</a>, a weekly civic-tech meetup focused on open-data projects. I built tools using transit APIs and GTFS feeds, which gave me a closer look at how institutional decisions shape the data transit agencies publish.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="advocacy-heading">
    <h2 id="advocacy-heading">Advocacy</h2>
    <p>Involved in transit and active transportation advocacy through the <a href="https://www.railpassengers.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rail Passengers Association</a>, <a href="https://www.ridersalliance.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Riders Alliance</a> (New York), and <a href="https://www.transalt.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Transportation Alternatives</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="interests-heading">
    <h2 id="interests-heading">Research Interests</h2>
    <p>Transit-oriented development — how land use, housing, and mobility connect, and what makes it actually work in practice. Climate adaptation in urban transport, and how policy can drive system-wide resilience rather than piecemeal fixes.</p>
  </section>

  </div>

</Base>
